<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — AgShare field DOWNLOADER dialog (Avalonia view).

    1:1 parity reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/Field/FormAgShareDownloader`
    (FormAgShareDownloader.cs + FormAgShareDownloader.Designer.cs, 334 lines). The dialog lists
    the user's own AgShare fields on the left, previews the selected field's boundary / AB-line
    geometry on the right, and offers download controls (get-selected, get-all with a progress
    bar, and a force-overwrite toggle). Per AAP §0.3.3 this is visual + behavioural FIDELITY to the
    current Windows Forms look, never a redesign: the same 1157 x 693 client area and the same
    absolute control layout, field for field.

    Wiring contract — the partner code-behind FormAgShareDownloaderView.axaml.cs
    (partial class AgOpenGPS.Views.FormAgShareDownloaderView : Window, constructed with the FormGPS
    context) owns ALL behaviour:
      * This is a CODE-BEHIND view, NOT MVVM — intentionally NO x:DataType, NO DataContext and
        NO {Binding} against a view-model. Every control is addressed imperatively by x:Name
        (mirroring the original WinForms partial, which used direct field access). The code-behind
        attaches the SelectedIndexChanged / Click handlers and runs the async download work by
        name, so NO event handlers are wired in this markup (the established sibling convention —
        see FormAgShareSettingsView, also a code-behind view in this migration).
      * lbFields is populated by the code-behind: it adds one GetOwnFieldDto per row (the DTO is the
        item's backing object), and the ItemTemplate below shows each field's Name. Selection is
        read back via lbFields.SelectedItem (single-select). The {Binding Name} in the template is a
        classic reflection binding against the row object (no x:DataType), exactly the pattern the
        sibling list dialogs (e.g. Pickers/FormFilePickerView) use.
      * previewHost is an intentionally EMPTY Border. The WinForms original hosted an
        OpenTK.GLControl (glControl1) and cleared it to an anthracite colour, then drew boundaries
        (lime), curves (red dashed) and AB lines (orange dashed). There is NO GL host control in
        Avalonia, so per the AAP the code-behind injects a NATIVE Avalonia preview control that
        renders the same geometry with a DrawingContext and assigns it as this Border's Child. The
        Border therefore carries only the dark anthracite background (matching the source clear
        colour) so the area reads correctly before the preview control is attached.
      * lblDownloading and progressBarDownloadAll start hidden (WinForms constructor set
        Visible = false); the code-behind reveals them during a get-all download and hides them
        afterwards. lblSelectedField is recoloured red by the code-behind when a field is selected.
      * The three command buttons and the force-overwrite checkbox are disabled by the code-behind
        for the duration of a get-all download, hence the :disabled style override below.

    Window shell mirrors FormAgShareDownloader.Designer.cs:
      Text "Download Fields From AgShare" -> Title (design-time placeholder; the code-behind sets
                                             gStr.gsAgShareDownloader at runtime)
      ClientSize 1157 x 693               -> Width / Height (Canvas matches the client area exactly)
      FormBorderStyle Fixed3D             -> CanResize="True" (the AAP standard for the re-platformed
                                             dialogs; the OS supplies the window chrome)
      StartPosition CenterParent          -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" (shown owned by FormGPS)
      ShowInTaskbar = false               -> ShowInTaskbar="False"
      BackColor (system default)          -> Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}" per the AAP,
                                             so the dialog tracks the day/night theme defined in App.axaml.

    Theme + assets:
      Background and text use the day/night brushes from App.axaml's ThemeDictionaries via
      DynamicResource (AogFrameBrush window chrome, AogTextBrush legible text in both Light and Dark).
      previewHost stays a FIXED anthracite (#FF1F1F1F == the source's 0.12 grey GL clear colour), not
      a theme brush, because it represents the renderer surface. Button glyphs are served from the GPS
      assembly (assembly name "AgOpenGPS") via avares:// URIs — the same btnImages/ assets the sibling
      GPS Avalonia views consume; casing verified against the files on disk in SourceCode/GPS/btnImages/
      (DownloadAll.png, DownloadAndUse.png, ForceOverwrite.png, OK64.png — all native 64 x 64).
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormAgShareDownloaderView"
        Title="Download Fields From AgShare"
        Width="1157"
        Height="693"
        CanResize="True"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}">

    <Window.Styles>
        <!--
            Flat, chrome-less image buttons reproduce the WinForms FlatStyle.Flat +
            FlatAppearance.BorderSize = 0 + transparent surface: only the glyph (and optional caption)
            shows, with no button fill in any visual state. The :pointerover / :pressed / :disabled
            template overrides suppress the Fluent hover / press / disabled background that would
            otherwise box the content. :disabled is included because the code-behind disables these
            buttons for the duration of a get-all download (same technique as the sibling
            FormWebCamView, whose buttons also start disabled).
        -->
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>

        <!--
            chkForceOverwrite reproduces the WinForms CheckBox with Appearance.Button: a flat,
            image-above-text toggle with NO separate check glyph and a salmon fill when checked
            (FlatAppearance.CheckedBackColor = LightSalmon). A minimal control template (a Border
            wrapping the content presenter) gives the button-like surface while keeping it a real
            CheckBox, so the code-behind's IsChecked read/write is unaffected. Unchecked == transparent,
            checked == LightSalmon (#FFFFA07A), exactly mirroring the source.
        -->
        <Style Selector="CheckBox.overwriteToggle">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <Border Name="tglBorder"
                            Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                            BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                            BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                            CornerRadius="3">
                        <ContentPresenter Name="PART_ContentPresenter"
                                          Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                          ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding ContentTemplate}"
                                          Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                                          HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                                          VerticalContentAlignment="Center" />
                    </Border>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="CheckBox.overwriteToggle:checked /template/ Border#tglBorder">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="#FFFFA07A" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="CheckBox.overwriteToggle:disabled">
            <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.5" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        The WinForms client area is 1157 x 693 with absolute (Location/Size) positioning, so the root
        is a Canvas and every child is placed by Canvas.Left / Canvas.Top at its exact Designer
        Width / Height. Point sizes are converted to device-independent pixels (pt x 96/72): the list
        Tahoma 18pt -> 24, lblSelectedField 15.75pt -> 21, lblDownloading 14.25pt -> 19, and the
        button/checkbox captions 9.75pt -> 13.
    -->
    <Canvas Width="1157" Height="693">

        <!--
            lbFields — WinForms ListView (View.Details, single "Field" column, MultiSelect = false,
            BackColor LightGreen, Tahoma 18pt) reimplemented as a single-select ListBox @ (12,12)
            492 x 567. The code-behind adds GetOwnFieldDto rows; the template shows each field's Name.
            Item text is forced dark so it stays legible on the fixed LightGreen surface in both themes.
        -->
        <ListBox x:Name="lbFields"
                 Canvas.Left="12" Canvas.Top="12"
                 Width="492" Height="567"
                 Background="LightGreen"
                 BorderThickness="0"
                 FontFamily="Tahoma"
                 FontSize="24"
                 SelectionMode="Single">
            <ListBox.ItemTemplate>
                <DataTemplate>
                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Name}"
                               Foreground="Black"
                               VerticalAlignment="Center"
                               TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                </DataTemplate>
            </ListBox.ItemTemplate>
        </ListBox>

        <!--
            previewHost — replaces the WinForms OpenTK.GLControl (glControl1 @ (510,12) 654 x 567,
            BorderStyle Fixed3D). Intentionally EMPTY: the code-behind injects a native Avalonia
            preview control (DrawingContext-based, NOT OpenGL) as this Border's Child. The fixed
            anthracite background (#FF1F1F1F) matches the source GL clear colour so the surface reads
            correctly before/behind the injected control.
        -->
        <Border x:Name="previewHost"
                Canvas.Left="510" Canvas.Top="12"
                Width="654" Height="567"
                Background="#FF1F1F1F"
                BorderBrush="#FF555555"
                BorderThickness="1" />

        <!--
            lblSelectedField — WinForms Label @ (12,592) 460 x 25, Microsoft Sans Serif 15.75pt Bold,
            AutoEllipsis. Default text "Selected Field:"; the code-behind replaces it with
            "Selected Field: <name>" and recolours it red on selection. AogTextBrush keeps the design-time
            text legible against the themed window background in both day and night.
        -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblSelectedField"
                   Canvas.Left="12" Canvas.Top="592"
                   Width="460" Height="25"
                   FontFamily="Microsoft Sans Serif"
                   FontSize="21"
                   FontWeight="Bold"
                   Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                   Text="Selected Field:"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />

        <!--
            chkForceOverwrite — WinForms CheckBox (Appearance.Button) @ (482,585) 92 x 105, image
            (ForceOverwrite, 64 x 64) above the "Overwrite" caption (TextImageRelation.ImageAboveText,
            TextAlign BottomCenter). The code-behind sets the caption from gStr.gsForceOverwrite. The
            overwriteToggle template (above) gives the flat button look + LightSalmon checked fill.
        -->
        <CheckBox x:Name="chkForceOverwrite"
                  Classes="overwriteToggle"
                  Canvas.Left="482" Canvas.Top="585"
                  Width="92" Height="105">
            <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                        Spacing="2">
                <Image Width="64" Height="64"
                       Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/ForceOverwrite.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
                <TextBlock Text="Overwrite"
                           FontFamily="Microsoft Sans Serif"
                           FontSize="13"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                           TextAlignment="Center"
                           TextWrapping="Wrap" />
            </StackPanel>
        </CheckBox>

        <!--
            btnSaveAll — WinForms Button @ (583,585) 94 x 105, flat, image (DownloadAll, 64 x 64) above
            the "Get All" caption. Click downloads every field (BtnDownloadAll_Click); the code-behind
            sets the caption from gStr.gsDownloadAll and wires the handler by name.
        -->
        <Button x:Name="btnSaveAll"
                Classes="imageButton"
                Canvas.Left="583" Canvas.Top="585"
                Width="94" Height="105">
            <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                        Spacing="2">
                <Image Width="64" Height="64"
                       Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/DownloadAll.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
                <TextBlock Text="Get All"
                           FontFamily="Microsoft Sans Serif"
                           FontSize="13"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                           TextAlignment="Center"
                           TextWrapping="Wrap" />
            </StackPanel>
        </Button>

        <!--
            lblDownloading — WinForms Label @ (678,592) 259 x 24, Microsoft Sans Serif 14.25pt Bold.
            Hidden by default (WinForms constructor Visible = false); the code-behind reveals it during
            a get-all download and sets its text from gStr ("Downloading... Please Wait").
        -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblDownloading"
                   Canvas.Left="678" Canvas.Top="592"
                   Width="259" Height="24"
                   FontFamily="Microsoft Sans Serif"
                   FontSize="19"
                   FontWeight="Bold"
                   Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                   Text="Downloading...Please Wait"
                   IsVisible="False"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center" />

        <!--
            progressBarDownloadAll — WinForms ProgressBar @ (683,628) 289 x 23. Hidden by default; the
            code-behind sets Maximum to the field count, reveals it, and drives Value during a get-all
            download via an IProgress callback.
        -->
        <ProgressBar x:Name="progressBarDownloadAll"
                     Canvas.Left="683" Canvas.Top="628"
                     Width="289" Height="23"
                     Minimum="0"
                     Maximum="100"
                     Value="0"
                     IsVisible="False" />

        <!--
            btnGetSelected — WinForms Button @ (978,585) 83 x 105, flat, image (DownloadAndUse, 64 x 64)
            above the "Get Selected" caption. Click downloads + opens the selected field (btnOpen_Click);
            the code-behind sets the caption from gStr.gsGetSelected and wires the handler by name.
        -->
        <Button x:Name="btnGetSelected"
                Classes="imageButton"
                Canvas.Left="978" Canvas.Top="585"
                Width="83" Height="105">
            <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                        Spacing="2">
                <Image Width="64" Height="64"
                       Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/DownloadAndUse.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
                <TextBlock Text="Get Selected"
                           FontFamily="Microsoft Sans Serif"
                           FontSize="13"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                           TextAlignment="Center"
                           TextWrapping="Wrap" />
            </StackPanel>
        </Button>

        <!--
            btnClose — WinForms Button @ (1067,596) 83 x 84, flat, image only (OK64, 64 x 64), no caption.
            Click closes the dialog (btnClose_Click); the code-behind wires the handler by name.
        -->
        <Button x:Name="btnClose"
                Classes="imageButton"
                Canvas.Left="1067" Canvas.Top="596"
                Width="83" Height="84"
                HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                VerticalContentAlignment="Center">
            <Image Width="64" Height="64"
                   Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/OK64.png"
                   Stretch="Uniform"
                   HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        </Button>

    </Canvas>
</Window>
